01:42.980 --> 01:43.980
Hi, Oz.

01:43.980 --> 01:44.980
Hi, Oz.

01:44.980 --> 01:45.980
Oh, hi, fellas.

01:45.980 --> 01:47.980
We thought we'd drop over and get our signals straight for tomorrow.

01:47.980 --> 01:48.980
Oh, no you didn't.

01:48.980 --> 01:51.980
You came over to help yourselves to some of my favorite lures.

01:51.980 --> 01:53.980
Now, Oz, you know us better than that.

01:53.980 --> 01:56.980
We'll let you cart them up to the lake and then we'll help ourselves.

01:56.980 --> 01:59.980
I don't care what you do as long as we catch some fish.

01:59.980 --> 02:01.980
Don't worry, we will.

02:01.980 --> 02:03.980
What time are you going to pick me up?

02:03.980 --> 02:05.980
I thought you were going to pick me up. I drove last time.

02:05.980 --> 02:07.980
And I drove the time before.

02:07.980 --> 02:12.980
Okay, then we'll pass for it.

02:12.980 --> 02:16.980
Okay, I'll pick you guys up.

02:16.980 --> 02:18.980
You're not going to use this one, are you?

02:18.980 --> 02:20.980
Well, you're darn right I am. Why not?

02:20.980 --> 02:23.980
The last time you used it, you scared all the fish away.

02:23.980 --> 02:26.980
You guys are just jealous. I've caught a lot of fish with this.

02:26.980 --> 02:28.980
Well, anyway, what time are you going to pick us up?

02:28.980 --> 02:30.980
Oh, how about, say, 5.30?

02:30.980 --> 02:33.980
5.30? The fish won't even be up that early.

02:33.980 --> 02:35.980
Well, it takes a couple of hours to drive up there.

02:35.980 --> 02:39.980
Two hours to drive to Lake Warfield? It only takes about 40 minutes.

02:39.980 --> 02:40.980
Who said anything about Lake Warfield?

02:40.980 --> 02:42.980
That's where we're going.

02:42.980 --> 02:44.980
Well, since when? When did we decide this?

02:44.980 --> 02:45.980
On the way over here.

02:45.980 --> 02:47.980
Well, thanks a lot. Who cast my ballot?

02:47.980 --> 02:49.980
What difference does it make? Joe wants to go up there.

02:49.980 --> 02:51.980
I want to go up there. That's two out of three.

02:51.980 --> 02:53.980
Besides, what's wrong with Lake Warfield?

02:53.980 --> 02:56.980
Well, it's fine if you want to pick wildflowers.

02:56.980 --> 02:59.980
But if you want to catch fish, I can think of a lot of better places.

02:59.980 --> 03:00.980
Name one.

03:00.980 --> 03:02.980
Wait a second. What are you doing?

03:02.980 --> 03:06.980
The last time he suggested a place, there wasn't even any water up there.

03:06.980 --> 03:11.980
Okay, you guys, but I happen to know the most sensational fishing spot in this section of the country.

03:11.980 --> 03:15.980
Oz, we've already decided we're going to Lake Warfield.

03:15.980 --> 03:18.980
They just stocked the place a couple of months ago, and there's bound to be a lot of fish.

03:18.980 --> 03:21.980
Well, I'd like to come home with some decent-sized fish for a change.

03:21.980 --> 03:24.980
Well, so would we. That's why we're going to Lake Warfield.

03:24.980 --> 03:26.980
Come on, Oz. Don't be so stubborn.

03:26.980 --> 03:29.980
Who's being stubborn? You guys are the ones who are being stubborn.

03:29.980 --> 03:32.980
Well, Joseph, am I being stubborn?

03:32.980 --> 03:34.980
Certainly not, am I?

03:34.980 --> 03:36.980
Not in the least.

03:36.980 --> 03:37.980
There, you see, Oz?

03:37.980 --> 03:40.980
All I see is a couple of guys who aren't going to catch any fish.

03:40.980 --> 03:42.980
Oh, that's what you think.

03:42.980 --> 03:45.980
Look, it's pretty obvious nobody's going to convince anybody around here,

03:45.980 --> 03:50.980
so why don't you guys go fishing where you want to go, and I'll go fishing where I want to go.

03:50.980 --> 03:51.980
Okay, we will.

03:51.980 --> 03:52.980
Okay.

03:52.980 --> 03:54.980
Now, wait a minute, Joe. We can't do that.

03:54.980 --> 03:55.980
We can't do what?

03:55.980 --> 04:01.980
We can't let Oz get up at 5.30 in the morning and drive up all alone to some place where there aren't any fish.

04:01.980 --> 04:03.980
Aren't any fish?

04:03.980 --> 04:04.980
Look, I'll tell you what I'll do.

04:04.980 --> 04:09.980
You guys, with your wives, of course, are invited over to our house for a trout dinner tomorrow night,

04:09.980 --> 04:11.980
and I'll supply the trout.

04:11.980 --> 04:12.980
We accept.

04:12.980 --> 04:13.980
What time?

04:13.980 --> 04:14.980
Say, 7 o'clock?

04:14.980 --> 04:15.980
You've got a deal.

04:15.980 --> 04:16.980
Okay.

04:16.980 --> 04:23.980
Oh, and Oz, be sure you have lots of onions for the hamburgers.

04:23.980 --> 04:24.980
Hi, boys.

04:24.980 --> 04:25.980
Hi, Pop.

04:25.980 --> 04:27.980
Say, do you guys have any plans for tomorrow?

04:27.980 --> 04:28.980
No, thanks, Pop.

04:28.980 --> 04:29.980
No, thanks, Pop.

04:29.980 --> 04:31.980
What do you mean, no thanks, Pop?

04:31.980 --> 04:33.980
I haven't even told you what I have in mind yet.

04:33.980 --> 04:36.980
Well, we know what you have in mind, and we don't want to get up at 5.30.

04:36.980 --> 04:37.980
Harriet?

04:37.980 --> 04:40.980
No, thanks, I don't want to get up at 5.30.

04:40.980 --> 04:43.980
I wish you people would let me ask the question before you turn me down.

04:43.980 --> 04:48.980
Look, why don't you just call up Joe and Darb and tell them you decided to go with them after all?

04:48.980 --> 04:50.980
Well, you know I can't do that, Harriet.

04:50.980 --> 04:57.980
After I made such a big issue about catching the trout and inviting them over for dinner.

04:57.980 --> 04:58.980
Whose dog is that?

04:58.980 --> 05:03.980
I don't know, but I'm sure he doesn't want to get up at 5.30 either.

05:03.980 --> 05:04.980
Well, good night.

05:04.980 --> 05:06.980
Oh, you're going to bed so early?

05:06.980 --> 05:07.980
Yeah.

05:07.980 --> 05:09.980
If I go to bed right now, I'll only get about seven hours sleep.

05:09.980 --> 05:10.980
Oh, well, good night, dear.

05:10.980 --> 05:39.980
Good night.

05:39.980 --> 05:41.980
I thought you went to bed.

05:41.980 --> 05:43.980
Well, I did, but I can't get to sleep.

05:43.980 --> 05:45.980
That dog has been barking for the last hour.

05:45.980 --> 05:47.980
Oh, that's on television.

05:47.980 --> 05:50.980
I've been watching The Hound of the Baskervilles.

05:50.980 --> 05:52.980
It's a real live dog.

05:52.980 --> 05:55.980
Turn it down a second.

05:55.980 --> 05:57.980
Oh, yeah.

05:57.980 --> 05:58.980
It's been going on like that for an hour.

05:58.980 --> 06:00.980
I wonder who he belongs to.

06:00.980 --> 06:03.980
Well, some people moved in that house down the street the other day.

06:03.980 --> 06:04.980
It could belong to them.

06:04.980 --> 06:06.980
Well, I wish they'd keep him quiet.

06:06.980 --> 06:07.980
Oh, he'll probably quiet down.

06:07.980 --> 06:09.980
Well, I hope so.

06:09.980 --> 06:20.980
I have to get up in about six hours.

06:20.980 --> 06:21.980
Hello?

06:21.980 --> 06:22.980
Oz, this is Joe.

06:22.980 --> 06:23.980
Oh, hi, Joe.

06:23.980 --> 06:25.980
Oz, you have a dog.

06:25.980 --> 06:26.980
You know we don't.

06:26.980 --> 06:27.980
Well, I hear one barking.

06:27.980 --> 06:29.980
It sounds like it's coming from over your way.

06:29.980 --> 06:33.980
Oh, well, I think it belongs to the people who just moved in down the street from us.

06:33.980 --> 06:34.980
I hear it on the phone.

06:34.980 --> 06:36.980
Sounds like it's right in your house.

06:36.980 --> 06:40.980
No, that's the hound of the Baskervilles.

06:40.980 --> 06:43.980
What is it, some kind of a practical joke or something?

06:43.980 --> 06:45.980
I tell you, it's not my dog.

06:45.980 --> 06:46.980
I'm trying to get to sleep.

06:46.980 --> 06:48.980
I'm going fishing in the morning.

06:48.980 --> 07:02.980
Well, so am I, and stop being such a grouch.

07:02.980 --> 07:03.980
You don't need to be quiet.

07:03.980 --> 07:05.980
I'm wide awake.

07:05.980 --> 07:08.980
It's a shame.

07:08.980 --> 07:12.980
All I can hear is that darn dog barking.

07:12.980 --> 07:16.980
I'm amazed you can hear anything.

07:16.980 --> 07:17.980
I think I ought to go over there.

07:17.980 --> 07:18.980
Where?

07:18.980 --> 07:19.980
Over to their house.

07:19.980 --> 07:21.980
Well, you can't do that.

07:21.980 --> 07:24.980
I can't go over and ask them to stop their dog from barking?

07:24.980 --> 07:26.980
Well, they might be asleep.

07:26.980 --> 07:28.980
Are you kidding? With all that going on?

07:28.980 --> 07:29.980
Well, now, that's not very nice.

07:29.980 --> 07:30.980
We don't even know the people.

07:30.980 --> 07:32.980
Come on, you get to sleep.

07:32.980 --> 07:45.980
You'll find out.

07:45.980 --> 07:46.980
Oh, that's beautiful.

07:46.980 --> 07:50.980
Now he's bringing in reinforcements.

07:50.980 --> 08:14.980
You get to sleep.

08:14.980 --> 08:16.980
Harriet.

08:16.980 --> 08:19.980
I'm going over there and see what I can do about this.

08:19.980 --> 08:20.980
Okay, dear, good luck.

08:20.980 --> 08:24.980
Catch lots of fish.

08:24.980 --> 08:35.980
She sleeps through anything.

08:35.980 --> 08:37.980
Hi there, boy.

08:37.980 --> 08:39.980
You been doing all that barking?

08:39.980 --> 08:41.980
Have you been doing all that barking, huh?

08:41.980 --> 08:53.980
Hey, you're a nice fella.

08:53.980 --> 08:54.980
Yes?

08:54.980 --> 08:55.980
Good evening.

08:55.980 --> 08:56.980
My name is Nelson.

08:56.980 --> 08:57.980
I'm your neighbor.

08:57.980 --> 08:58.980
I live just down the street.

08:58.980 --> 08:59.980
Oh, good evening.

08:59.980 --> 09:00.980
I'm Mrs. Fraser.

09:00.980 --> 09:02.980
I'm glad to see I didn't wake you up.

09:02.980 --> 09:03.980
Oh, no, no.

09:03.980 --> 09:04.980
I was watching the late show.

09:04.980 --> 09:08.980
Oh, well, your dog was barking, and I thought maybe something was wrong.

09:08.980 --> 09:09.980
Oh, I'm sorry.

09:09.980 --> 09:12.980
I've tried everything, but he just won't stop.

09:12.980 --> 09:14.980
I hope he hasn't been disturbing you.

09:14.980 --> 09:19.980
Oh, well, it isn't that, but a couple of my neighbors are going fishing tomorrow,

09:19.980 --> 09:23.980
and you know how it is when you have to get up early in the morning.

09:23.980 --> 09:24.980
Hiya, boy.

09:24.980 --> 09:25.980
Oh, his name's Charlie.

09:25.980 --> 09:26.980
Oh, hiya, Charlie.

09:26.980 --> 09:30.980
Well, I guess it's the new surroundings, and I think he probably misses my husband.

09:30.980 --> 09:31.980
He's away on a business trip.

09:31.980 --> 09:33.980
Oh, I see.

09:33.980 --> 09:35.980
Charlie's always been kind of a man's dog.

09:35.980 --> 09:36.980
Oh, yeah.

09:36.980 --> 09:38.980
Well, he seems to be quiet now.

09:38.980 --> 09:39.980
I guess that must be it.

09:39.980 --> 09:40.980
Well, I hope he stays that way.

09:40.980 --> 09:42.980
He's usually very well behaved.

09:42.980 --> 09:44.980
Hi, boy.

09:44.980 --> 09:46.980
Well, I guess I'll be going.

09:46.980 --> 09:47.980
Good night.

09:47.980 --> 09:48.980
Good night, Mr. Nelson.

09:48.980 --> 09:50.980
Oh, and thank you for stopping by.

09:50.980 --> 09:51.980
You bet.

09:54.980 --> 09:56.980
Now, Charlie, cut it out.

09:58.980 --> 10:00.980
Charlie, stop that.

10:01.980 --> 10:02.980
Stop that, Charlie.

10:02.980 --> 10:04.980
Now, you cut it out, Charlie.

10:04.980 --> 10:06.980
You cut it out now.

10:06.980 --> 10:07.980
You be a good boy.

10:07.980 --> 10:09.980
Now, no, no, you stay there now.

10:09.980 --> 10:10.980
Be a good boy.

10:10.980 --> 10:12.980
He seems to like you.

10:12.980 --> 10:13.980
Yeah.

10:13.980 --> 10:14.980
Well, good night.

10:14.980 --> 10:15.980
Good night.

10:30.980 --> 10:31.980
Ozzie?

10:31.980 --> 10:32.980
Yeah.

10:32.980 --> 10:33.980
Where have you been?

10:33.980 --> 10:35.980
I went over to see about the dog.

10:35.980 --> 10:36.980
Oh.

10:36.980 --> 10:37.980
Well, I guess you're right.

10:37.980 --> 10:39.980
He seems to have stopped barking.

10:39.980 --> 10:40.980
Oh, yeah.

10:40.980 --> 10:41.980
Well, you better get to bed.

10:41.980 --> 10:43.980
You're not going to get any sleep at all.

10:43.980 --> 10:47.980
Uh, Harriet, uh, we have a little problem.

10:47.980 --> 10:48.980
What do you mean?

10:48.980 --> 10:51.980
Um, what are we going to do about Charlie?

10:51.980 --> 10:53.980
Charlie.

11:05.980 --> 11:08.980
Everybody's doing it, jumping for joy.

11:08.980 --> 11:10.980
Mmm, boy, almond joy.

