Almonds, chocolate, and malted milk.

11:59.980 --> 12:02.980
That's Peter Paul Almond Cluster.

12:08.980 --> 12:10.980
Want some more hot chocolate?

12:10.980 --> 12:12.980
Uh, no thanks. I have to get up to bed.

12:12.980 --> 12:13.980
How about Charlie?

12:13.980 --> 12:15.980
He's had enough.

12:15.980 --> 12:18.980
You know, I realize it's late and I may be a little foggy,

12:18.980 --> 12:21.980
but I still don't understand how we ended up dog sitting for Mrs. Fraser.

12:21.980 --> 12:24.980
Well, it just seemed like the simplest solution.

12:24.980 --> 12:27.980
As I say, old Charlie's only happy when there's a man around,

12:27.980 --> 12:29.980
so I agreed to keep him here until morning.

12:29.980 --> 12:33.980
If he stayed over there, he'd just bark all night.

12:33.980 --> 12:35.980
Well, I'd better get up to bed.

12:35.980 --> 12:36.980
What about your friend?

12:36.980 --> 12:39.980
Well, I think he's okay now.

12:39.980 --> 12:40.980
Put him out in the backyard.

12:40.980 --> 12:43.980
Come on, Charlie.

12:44.980 --> 12:46.980
Don't forget to lock the gate.

12:46.980 --> 12:48.980
I locked it when I came back in.

12:48.980 --> 12:52.980
Good night, Charlie. See you in the morning.

12:53.980 --> 12:57.980
If you sleep fast, you can still get about four hours.

13:02.980 --> 13:04.980
Oh, great.

13:04.980 --> 13:07.980
Maybe it's too cold out there.

13:07.980 --> 13:10.980
Will you let him in? I'll get this.

13:10.980 --> 13:11.980
Hello?

13:11.980 --> 13:13.980
Would you keep your dog quiet?

13:13.980 --> 13:14.980
It's not my dog.

13:14.980 --> 13:18.980
Well, then somebody over there has a terrible cold.

13:18.980 --> 13:20.980
I'm keeping a neighbor's dog.

13:20.980 --> 13:21.980
Well, do something, will you?

13:21.980 --> 13:23.980
Will you relax, Joe?

13:23.980 --> 13:26.980
He's sitting right here beside me and he's nice and quiet now.

13:26.980 --> 13:29.980
Listen, you can hear him breathing.

13:29.980 --> 13:32.980
Breathe for Joe.

13:33.980 --> 13:36.980
Here's some water in case you get thirsty.

13:36.980 --> 13:40.980
And this is a nice soft blanket so you go to sleep like a good boy.

13:40.980 --> 13:42.980
Good night.

13:43.980 --> 13:44.980
I think he'll be okay now.

13:44.980 --> 13:46.980
You hope.

13:48.980 --> 13:49.980
Boy, I'm tired already.

13:49.980 --> 13:51.980
I'll bet you are.

13:51.980 --> 13:53.980
Why don't you just forget about fishing tomorrow?

13:53.980 --> 13:56.980
Oh, Harry, I can't do that.

13:59.980 --> 14:01.980
Well, the boys just drove up.

14:01.980 --> 14:06.980
Oh, yeah.

14:09.980 --> 14:13.980
Oh, great.

14:13.980 --> 14:32.980
Okay, Joe, I hear him.

14:32.980 --> 14:33.980
Nice paws.

14:33.980 --> 14:34.980
Nice paws, nice paws.

14:34.980 --> 14:42.980
Nice paws.

14:42.980 --> 14:47.980
Now, look, Charlie, you just lie there nice and quiet like a good boy.

14:47.980 --> 14:50.980
I have to get up in about three and a half hours.

14:50.980 --> 14:52.980
Now, let's all get some sleep, huh?

14:52.980 --> 15:21.980
Good luck.

15:23.980 --> 15:35.980
Charlie.

15:35.980 --> 15:53.980
Are you sure you're nice and comfortable, Charlie?

15:53.980 --> 15:59.980
Ozzie, 5.30.

15:59.980 --> 16:01.980
I can't believe it.

16:01.980 --> 16:02.980
You didn't have to get up.

16:02.980 --> 16:05.980
I did, too. You left the alarm on upstairs.

16:05.980 --> 16:09.980
Oh, I'm sorry.

16:09.980 --> 16:12.980
Look at him.

16:12.980 --> 16:15.980
Last night we couldn't make him go to sleep, and now look at him.

16:15.980 --> 16:18.980
Well, he's tired. You kept him awake all night.

16:18.980 --> 16:23.980
It's all the same to you. I'm going back to sleep. Have a good time.

16:23.980 --> 16:25.980
Hi, Mr. Nelson.

16:25.980 --> 16:26.980
Oh, hiya, Barry.

16:26.980 --> 16:28.980
What are you doing up so early in the morning?

16:28.980 --> 16:30.980
I always get up early.

16:30.980 --> 16:32.980
Oh, well, I guess it's okay if you're used to it.

16:32.980 --> 16:33.980
Mr. Nelson?

16:33.980 --> 16:34.980
Yeah?

16:34.980 --> 16:37.980
You look terrible this morning. What happened?

16:37.980 --> 16:40.980
Oh, well, I didn't get much sleep last night.

16:40.980 --> 16:41.980
Are you just getting home?

16:41.980 --> 16:43.980
No, I'm going fishing.

16:43.980 --> 16:45.980
Why don't you go back to bed?

16:45.980 --> 16:47.980
Well, it's kind of a long story.

16:47.980 --> 16:51.980
See, I have a bet with Mr. Randolph and Mr. Darby.

16:51.980 --> 16:53.980
I promised to bring them back a trout dinner.

16:53.980 --> 16:55.980
They were going fishing, too.

16:55.980 --> 16:56.980
That is, if they got up for it.

16:56.980 --> 16:58.980
They left a few minutes ago.

16:58.980 --> 17:00.980
Oh.

17:00.980 --> 17:02.980
Well, then I guess they managed to get up on time.

17:02.980 --> 17:04.980
How come you didn't go with them?

17:04.980 --> 17:08.980
Well, they wanted to go to Lake Warfield, and I wanted to go to Shadow Lake.

17:08.980 --> 17:10.980
See, the fishing's better up there.

17:10.980 --> 17:11.980
Well, I'd better get going.

17:11.980 --> 17:14.980
I hope you catch some fish before you fall asleep.

17:14.980 --> 17:17.980
Oh, I think I will. I'm wide awake now.

17:17.980 --> 17:19.980
Good luck, Mr. Nelson.

17:19.980 --> 17:20.980
Okay, so long, Barry.

17:20.980 --> 17:22.980
Bye.

17:22.980 --> 17:24.980
Charlie.

17:24.980 --> 17:29.980
Now, who let you out of the house, as if I didn't know?

17:29.980 --> 17:31.980
Come on.

17:31.980 --> 17:55.980
Stay there, boy.

17:55.980 --> 18:04.980
Stay there.

18:04.980 --> 18:05.980
Morning.

18:05.980 --> 18:07.980
Morning.

18:07.980 --> 18:09.980
A couple of black coffee, please.

18:09.980 --> 18:14.980
Okay.

18:14.980 --> 18:15.980
You going fishing?

18:15.980 --> 18:18.980
Well, I am if I can stay awake.

18:18.980 --> 18:23.980
You're not the only one having that trouble.

18:23.980 --> 18:24.980
When did they come in here?

18:24.980 --> 18:26.980
Oh, about ten minutes ago. Do you know them?

18:26.980 --> 18:29.980
Uh, well, they look kind of familiar.

18:29.980 --> 18:30.980
Do you think I ought to wake them up?

18:30.980 --> 18:34.980
Oh, no, I wouldn't if I were you. They probably need to sleep.

18:34.980 --> 18:51.980
Okay.

18:51.980 --> 18:52.980
Thank you.

18:52.980 --> 19:20.980
Bye.

19:20.980 --> 19:24.980
Uh, Joe?

19:24.980 --> 19:27.980
Oh, I must have dozed off.

19:27.980 --> 19:29.980
Me too.

19:29.980 --> 19:31.980
Well, come on, let's get going.

19:31.980 --> 19:36.980
I know this sounds crazy, but I thought I heard that darn dog barking again.

19:36.980 --> 19:39.980
Me too. But I thought I was dreaming.

19:39.980 --> 19:42.980
You don't suppose we could hear him all the way up here, do you?

19:42.980 --> 19:45.980
We're twenty miles from home.

19:45.980 --> 19:50.980
Well, just the same, he sure has a loud bark.

20:15.980 --> 20:30.980
He's gone.

20:30.980 --> 20:35.980
He's gone.

20:35.980 --> 20:46.980
He's gone.

21:06.980 --> 21:20.980
He's gone.

21:20.980 --> 21:49.980
He's gone.

21:49.980 --> 21:51.980
Yes, sir, may I help you?

21:51.980 --> 21:56.980
Uh, yes, uh, do you have any, do you have any trout?

21:56.980 --> 21:57.980
Yes, sir.

21:57.980 --> 22:00.980
I'd like a couple of nice ones that, that...

22:00.980 --> 22:02.980
That look like they've just been caught?

22:02.980 --> 22:03.980
Yes.

22:03.980 --> 22:06.980
Don't worry, sir, we handle this problem all the time. We won't say a word.

22:06.980 --> 22:08.980
I'll try to find you a couple of nice ones.

22:08.980 --> 22:09.980
Thank you.

22:09.980 --> 22:10.980
Hi, Mr. Nelson.

22:10.980 --> 22:12.980
Oh, hi there, Barry.

22:12.980 --> 22:14.980
Did you catch a lot of fish?

22:14.980 --> 22:16.980
Uh, well, not too many.

22:16.980 --> 22:19.980
How many did you catch?

22:19.980 --> 22:21.980
Uh, well, uh, none.

22:21.980 --> 22:26.980
I would have, except I fell asleep and somebody stole my fishing pole.

22:26.980 --> 22:27.980
How do these look?

22:27.980 --> 22:29.980
Oh, uh, very nice.

22:29.980 --> 22:31.980
Do you have your creel with you?

22:31.980 --> 22:33.980
Uh, no, it's out in the car.

22:33.980 --> 22:35.980
Oh, well, I'll just wrap them in plain paper.

22:35.980 --> 22:37.980
Thank you.

22:37.980 --> 22:39.980
Mr. Nelson?

22:39.980 --> 22:40.980
Yeah?

22:40.980 --> 22:43.980
Are you going to make believe you caught those?

22:43.980 --> 22:46.980
Uh, well, uh, not exactly.

22:46.980 --> 22:48.980
Uh, that is...

22:48.980 --> 22:52.980
See, actually, my contention was that the fishing was better at Shadow Lake.

22:52.980 --> 22:55.980
Uh, which it really is.

22:55.980 --> 22:58.980
Uh, uh, pardon me.

22:58.980 --> 23:02.980
Uh, uh, pardon me, uh, would you mind changing my order, please?

23:02.980 --> 23:05.980
I'd like to have three pounds of ground round instead.

23:05.980 --> 23:07.980
Yes, sir.

23:07.980 --> 23:08.980
Mr. Nelson?

23:08.980 --> 23:09.980
Yes?

23:09.980 --> 23:12.980
I like to shake hands with honest men.

23:12.980 --> 23:14.980
Oh, well, thank you, Barry.

23:14.980 --> 23:15.980
Me too, sir.

23:15.980 --> 23:16.980
Oh, thank you.

23:16.980 --> 23:18.980
Good show.

23:32.980 --> 23:35.980
You know, for a guy who didn't get any sleep last night, you certainly look well rested.

23:35.980 --> 23:36.980
Oh, thanks.

23:36.980 --> 23:37.980
Well, I took a shower.

23:37.980 --> 23:39.980
Besides, don't forget I slept all day.

23:39.980 --> 23:40.980
Hi.

23:40.980 --> 23:42.980
Oh, hi, Dave.

23:42.980 --> 23:43.980
Uh, did you take Charlie back?

23:43.980 --> 23:46.980
Yeah, Mrs. Fraser said thanks a lot for taking care of him.

23:46.980 --> 23:49.980
Oh, I sure hope he doesn't bark all night again tonight.

23:49.980 --> 23:52.980
Well, she said she was sure he wouldn't. Mr. Fraser's coming home tonight.

23:52.980 --> 23:53.980
Oh, that's good.

23:53.980 --> 23:55.980
Well, thanks a lot, Dave.

23:55.980 --> 23:56.980
Okay.

23:56.980 --> 23:59.980
Are you sure hamburgers will be all right for dinner?

23:59.980 --> 24:02.980
Are you kidding? They'll be too good for those guys.

24:02.980 --> 24:04.980
Gee, I sure wish I'd caught some fish.

24:04.980 --> 24:07.980
I bet I would have too if I hadn't fallen asleep.

24:07.980 --> 24:08.980
Oh, here they are.

24:08.980 --> 24:09.980
I'll get it.

24:09.980 --> 24:11.980
Gee, I hate to face them.

24:11.980 --> 24:13.980
I must admit I'm not a very good loser.

24:13.980 --> 24:14.980
Well, who is?

24:14.980 --> 24:15.980
Hi.

24:15.980 --> 24:16.980
Hi, Dave.

24:16.980 --> 24:17.980
Hi, Ozzie.

24:17.980 --> 24:18.980
Hi, Ozzie.

24:18.980 --> 24:19.980
Hi, Clara.

24:19.980 --> 24:20.980
Hi, Oz.

24:20.980 --> 24:21.980
Okay, Oz, let's see them.

24:21.980 --> 24:22.980
See what?

24:22.980 --> 24:23.980
All those big fish you caught.

24:23.980 --> 24:25.980
We're having trout for dinner, aren't we? That's what you promised.

24:25.980 --> 24:28.980
Okay, you guys are talking so big. How many fish did you catch?

24:28.980 --> 24:32.980
They caught three. They're home in our freezer in one ice tray.

24:32.980 --> 24:33.980
Clara.

24:33.980 --> 24:35.980
Oh, there's somebody at the back door. Pardon.

24:35.980 --> 24:41.980
Well, come on in and sit down.

24:41.980 --> 24:44.980
You know something, Joe? I'll bet he didn't catch a darn thing.

24:44.980 --> 24:47.980
I'll bet he didn't even go up there.

24:47.980 --> 24:48.980
Oh, hi, Mrs. Fraser. Come on in.

24:48.980 --> 24:52.980
Oh, thank you, but I have to get right back. My husband's waiting for his dinner.

24:52.980 --> 24:53.980
What's this?

24:53.980 --> 24:55.980
Well, it's a little thank you gift for taking such good care of Charlie.

24:55.980 --> 25:00.980
Oh, that wasn't necessary.

25:00.980 --> 25:04.980
Oh, what beautiful trout. Where'd you get these?

25:04.980 --> 25:05.980
My husband caught them.

25:05.980 --> 25:09.980
He loves to fish and he managed to sneak away for a few hours while he was on his trip.

25:09.980 --> 25:12.980
Oh, they're just beautiful. Thank you so much.

25:12.980 --> 25:13.980
Well, it was a pleasure. Goodbye, Mr. Hoffman.

25:13.980 --> 25:17.980
Goodbye.

25:17.980 --> 25:19.980
Okay, Oz, where are the fish?

25:19.980 --> 25:20.980
You mean the hamburgers?

25:20.980 --> 25:22.980
Wait a second.

25:22.980 --> 25:24.980
Holy smoke.

25:24.980 --> 25:26.980
Doggone you, Joe. I told you we should have gone with Oz.

25:26.980 --> 25:30.980
What are you talking about? You're the one who insisted on going up to that miserable mud hole.

25:30.980 --> 25:34.980
Come on, fellas.

25:34.980 --> 25:35.980
Oz, come on, tell us. Where'd you get the fish?

25:35.980 --> 25:36.980
Well, somebody gave them to me.

25:36.980 --> 25:40.980
Okay, very funny. Come on, where'd you go?

25:40.980 --> 25:43.980
Well, it's kind of a long story.

25:43.980 --> 25:44.980
Did you go up there alone?

25:44.980 --> 25:48.980
No, this big shaggy dog went up there with me.

25:48.980 --> 25:52.980
And we sat out in the sun for a while and we both fell asleep.

25:52.980 --> 25:54.980
Okay, you fellas, out of the kitchen. I have to finish dinner.

25:54.980 --> 25:56.980
Come on, Joe. We're getting nowhere fast.

25:56.980 --> 25:58.980
Oh, he's a nice fellow. He'll tell us later.

25:58.980 --> 26:00.980
Would you put these on the fire, please?

26:00.980 --> 26:01.980
Ozzie?

26:01.980 --> 26:03.980
Yes, dear?

26:03.980 --> 26:06.980
Never mind the yes, dear. Where'd you get these?

26:06.980 --> 26:11.980
Mrs. Fraser's husband caught them and she just brought them over and gave them to me for taking care of Charlie.

26:11.980 --> 26:13.980
Well, wasn't that nice of her?

26:13.980 --> 26:15.980
Did you tell Darvin, Joe?

26:15.980 --> 26:17.980
Well, I started to.

26:17.980 --> 26:20.980
I don't blame you.

26:20.980 --> 26:22.980
You think you can get them ready in time for dinner?

26:22.980 --> 26:23.980
Oh, I think so.

26:23.980 --> 26:26.980
What are we going to do with three pounds of ground round?

26:26.980 --> 26:33.980
Well, why not? He earned it.

26:33.980 --> 26:36.980
Coming right up, Charlie.

26:36.980 --> 26:57.980
You know, from now on, this is going to be my favorite shaggy dog story.

26:57.980 --> 27:08.980
In the afternoon, when things slow down, when you're wondering what to do.

27:08.980 --> 27:37.980
Let's go. Go bowling.

27:37.980 --> 27:49.980
Nothing brings people together or makes friends so fast as bowling.

27:49.980 --> 27:51.980
So call a friend.

27:51.980 --> 27:56.980
Bowl Brunswick tomorrow.

27:56.980 --> 28:03.980
Tonight's adventures of Ozzie and Harriet was brought to you by Brunswick.

28:03.980 --> 28:07.980
Brunswick, the leader in America's favorite family recreation.

28:07.980 --> 28:36.980
Brunswick, the number one name in bowling.

28:36.980 --> 29:04.980
Brunswick, the number one name in bowling.

